s catchphrase from the  comics and he's not the only one who  uses it Neymar and other atlanteans  frequently shout this phrase before  heading into battle despite being  created in 1939 Neymar wouldn't start  saying imperious wrecks until the 1960s  when he was reintroduced in a Fantastic  Four comic and it stuck ever since  eventually making its way into the most  recent Marvel flick every great comic  book character needs a catchphrase the  thing has it's  well the Hulk has an incredibly similar  line of his own  as far as battle cries go those are both  pretty straightforward they mean exactly  what they say but Neymar's big line is  leaving plenty of people confused about  what they're supposed to feel whenever  he shouts it once in the comics Neymar  attempted to provide some clarification  about what he means by the big line  detailing his reasoning in 2018's Thor  issue 1. in that book Thor spends a  while duking it out with Neymar during  the battle Neymar unleashes his  signature catchphrase to which Thor  responds in a surprising way saying all  these years Namor and I still have no  idea what that even means ever the  friendly foe Neymar decides to shed some  light on the situation by explaining it  means I'm going to feed your sorry ass  Guardian High to the biggest sharks I  can find which isn't exactly accurate  still that explanation does a pretty  good job of capturing the essence of  what Neymar likely means whenever he  shouts his big line I've been saying it  for years and if you heard it that made  your ass  [Music]
 

